  "answer_text": "Here is a complete overview of the MLA and MP seats in **Telangana**:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f MLA Seats (State Legislature)\n\n### 1. Telangana Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha)\n- There are **119 MLAs** in the Legislative Assembly, elected by the people. The state is divided into **119 constituencies** with roughly equal populations.\n- The Telangana Legislative Assembly came into existence with 119 seats in **June 2014** with the formation of Telangana.\n\n### 2. Telangana Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad)\n- Elections take place to elect **40 members** to the Legislative Council, of whom 14 are elected by members of the Telangana Legislative Assembly, 14 by local authorities, 6 nominated by the Governor, 3 elected by teachers, and 3 elected by graduates. Members hold their seats for **six years**.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdf\ufe0f MP Seats (Parliament)\n\n### 1. Lok Sabha (Lower House)\n- Telangana has **17 Lok Sabha constituencies**, with 3 reserved for Scheduled Castes (SC) and 2 for Scheduled Tribes (ST).\n\n### 2. Rajya Sabha (Upper House)\n- Telangana has **7 Rajya Sabha seats**.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcca Summary Table\n\n| House | Type | Total Seats |\n|---|---|---|\n| Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha) | State (MLA) | **119** |\n| Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad) | State (MLC) | **40** |\n| Lok Sabha | Parliament (MP) | **17** |\n| Rajya Sabha | Parliament (MP) | **7** |\n| **Total MPs** | | **24** |\n\nSo in total, Telangana has **119 MLA seats**, **40 MLC seats**, **17 Lok Sabha MP seats**, and **7 Rajya Sabha MP seats**.",
